## 1. kubectl create namespace production

## 2. helm repo add external-secrets https://charts.external-secrets.io

helm repo update
helm install external-secrets \
 external-secrets/external-secrets \
 -n external-secrets \
 --create-namespace

kubectl get pods -n external-secrets
kubectl get crd | grep external-secrets
externalsecrets.external-secrets.io
secretstores.external-secrets.io
clustersecretstores.external-secrets.io

## 3. Create the AWS Secrets Manager secret with name:

production/myapp/mysql

    username
    password
    host
    database

So in AWS Secrets Manager, create a secret whose value is JSON similar to:
{
"username": "admin",
"password": "MyStrongPassword123!",
"host": "mysql.production.svc.cluster.local",
"database": "myapp"
}
